// TEST: Tuple Width And Component Types Cannot Mix (rejects)
// ERROR: BL1004
// ERROR-CONTAINS: cannot be mixed
// `Tuple<...>` disambiguates on the WHOLE argument list: a single integer
// literal is a width, anything else is a component-type list. A list holding
// both is neither, so it is refused outright rather than silently given one
// of the two readings -- there is no reading of "3" as a type and none of
// `Float64` as a width.
//
// Both orders are caught (the components are parsed by a hand-rolled loop
// rather than `sepBy`, precisely so an integer in ANY position gets this
// message instead of the generic "unexpected token in type").
function g(p: Tuple<3, Float64>) -> Float64 = p[0]
// EXPECT: parse failure -- a width and a component list cannot be mixed
